WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.440
Knowing this two by two confusion&nbsp;
matrix is just the beginning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.760
There are many different metrics can be derived&nbsp;
from those basic metrics. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.400
many metrics can be derived by taking ratios&nbsp;
of different numbers from this basic metrics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.560
First, let's introduce a set of metrics that are&nbsp;
derived by normalizing some terms with the ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.600
truth value, either the total population or the&nbsp;
condition positive or the condition negative.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.040
All these metrics are defined by some&nbsp;
conative divided by those normalization terms.&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.600
&nbsp;
For example, accuracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.560
is the ratio from the sum of true positive and&nbsp;
true negative divided by the total population.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.760
Accuracy is the most basic metric that&nbsp;
many people have intuitive understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:52.240
but accuracy is not always the best measure when&nbsp;
the class label are very imbalanced. If only 1%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:58.320
of the total population have heart failure, models&nbsp;
can be achieved 99% accuracy by simply predicting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.760
everyone would not have heart failure. So, it&nbsp;
is important to use the appropriate metric for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.960
measuring the performance of a predictive model.
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.360
Another important metric is true positive rate or&nbsp;
sensitivity or recall. They have different names,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.840
because the same metric has been developed by&nbsp;
different communities, and true positive rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.680
equals the true positive divided by the&nbsp;
condition positive in the ground truth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.680
To explain the intuition, let's assume positive&nbsp;
means heart failure and negative means without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.920
heart failure. The intuition of true positive rate&nbsp;
is to measure among all people with heart failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.880
what percentage is correctly&nbsp;
identified by the predictive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.160
model?
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:43.520
A very related metric can be derived called&nbsp;
false negative rate, which equals 1 minus true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:49.280
positive rate. The intuition of false negative&nbsp;
rate is among all heart failure patients,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.360
what percentage of those patients is missed by the&nbsp;
predicting model? False positive rate is the ratio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.440
between false positive and the condition negative.&nbsp;
The intuition of false positive rate is to measure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.080
among all people without heart failure, what&nbsp;
percentage of them is incorrectly predicted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.800
the model as to have heart failure?
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.440
Finally, true negative rate or specificity&nbsp;
is the number of true negative divided by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.080
the ground truth condition negative, which&nbsp;
also equals 1 minus false positive rate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.840
The intuition behind true negative rate is to&nbsp;
find among all people without heart failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.840
what percentage of them is correctly&nbsp;
classified as non-heart failure patients?&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.120
&nbsp;
Note that accuracy measures the combination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.000
performance of true positive and true negative,&nbsp;
while true positive rate measures the performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.880
only about true positive, and true negative rate&nbsp;
measures the performance only about true negative.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.560
It is often possible to obtain high performance&nbsp;
on a single metrics such as accuracy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.640
while it's difficult to obtain high performance on&nbsp;
all metrics. That's why we often test a predictive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.240
model against multiple metrics. First of all,&nbsp;
different metrics are designed for different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.840
situations. It is important to choose the&nbsp;
proper metric for your prediction study.

